.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt JG-TYPEWRITE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jg-typewrite
.Nd generate TypeScript declaration files from JSDoc annotations
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl d Ar type name body
.Op Fl e Ar exclude
.Op Fl h Ar header
.Op Fl f Ar footer
.Ar \.\.\.files
.
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.ad l
.Nm
extracts type annotations from JSDoc blocks in a list of source
.Ar files ,
generating a
.Dq Ar filename Ns Sy \.d.ts
file for each one.
Each type declaration is written on a single line,
making the files amenable to tooling like
.Xr cat 1
and
.Xr sort 1 .
.
.Pp
.\" Replace an aliased version of a JSDoc tag (\$1) with
.\" its "canonical" form stored in string named \$2.
.de jsdoc-dealias
.	ds \\$2 \&
.	if '\\$1'virtual'      .ds \\$2 abstract
.	if '\\$1'extends'      .ds \\$2 augments
.	if '\\$1'constructor'  .ds \\$2 class
.	if '\\$1'const'        .ds \\$2 constant
.	if '\\$1'defaultvalue' .ds \\$2 default
.	if '\\$1'desc'         .ds \\$2 description
.	if '\\$1'host'         .ds \\$2 external
.	if '\\$1'fileoverview' .ds \\$2 file
.	if '\\$1'overview'     .ds \\$2 file
.	if '\\$1'emits'        .ds \\$2 fires
.	if '\\$1'func'         .ds \\$2 function        
.	if '\\$1'method'       .ds \\$2 function
.	if '\\$1'var'          .ds \\$2 member
.	if '\\$1'arg'          .ds \\$2 param
.	if '\\$1'argument'     .ds \\$2 param
.	if '\\$1'prop'         .ds \\$2 property
.	if '\\$1'return'       .ds \\$2 returns
.	if '\\$1'exception'    .ds \\$2 throws
.	if '\\$1'yield'        .ds \\$2 yields
.	if '\\$1'linkcode'     .ds \\$2 link
.	if '\\$1'linkplain'    .ds \\$2 link
..
.de @
.	jsdoc-dealias \\$1 jsdoc-tag
.	ie t .Lk "https://jsdoc.app/tags-\\*[jsdoc-tag]" \f(CR@\\*[jsdoc-tag]\fP \&\\$2
.	el   .Sy @\\$1 \&\\$2
.	rm jsdoc-tag
..
The JSDoc markup parsed when called via
.Nm
is syntactically differently than normal JSDoc blocks.
These differences in syntax are to accommodate misuse of
.@ var
and
.@ property ,
sometimes used in lieu of
.@ enum
when synthesising enumerated types without a corresponding JavaScript member.
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width 6n
.It Fl d , Fl -declare Ar type name body
Add an additional type declaration to the file.
.Ar type
may be any exportable binding name
.Pq Sy const , let , type , interface , var No or Sy function ,
.Ar name
is the name of the declaration's subject,
and
.Ar body
is its definition,
possibly requiring quotes.
This option may be specified multiple times,
once per declaration.
.Pp
Combining this option with
.Fl -exclude
redefines a type declaration;
exclusion patterns don't extend to declarations specified via command-line.
.
.It Fl e , Fl -exclude Ar pattern
Regular expression matching the names of types to exclude from generated files.
.Pp
This option may be specified multiple times
to provide additional exclusion patterns,
only one of which need match a type's name for it to be filtered out.
.
.It Fl h , Fl -header Ar text
Prologue to prepend to each generated type declaration file.
.
.It Fl f , Fl -footer Ar text
Epilogue to append to each generated type declaration file.
.
.It Fl s , Fl -sort
Sort generated typings alphabetically.
.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a terse usage summary, then terminate.
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh FILES
The following file paths are relative to
.Nm jg Ap s
installation directory.
.
.ds to-ts jsdoc/to-typescript.mjs
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Pa jsdoc/config.json
JSDoc configuration file that initialises the plugins that do the heavy lifting.
Referenced automatically by the call to
.Ql jsdoc
made by
.Pa \*[to-ts] ,
which see.
.
.It Pa jsdoc/fix-props.cjs
JSDoc plugin to replace aberrant
.@ property
usage in incompatible contexts.
.
.It Pa jsdoc/fix-typedefs.cjs
JSDoc plugin to replace
.@ enum
tags with TypeScript unions,
among other tweaks related to
.@ typedef
tags.
.
.It Pa \*[to-ts]
Module that exports functions to perform the chaotic wrangling of JSDoc markup,
called directly from
.Nm .
.
.It Pa jsdoc/utils.cjs
Module that exports ancillary helper functions shared by
.Pa \*[to-ts]
and the aforementioned plugins.
.Pp
Most of these helper functions are specific to
.Nm Ap s
usage,
and are of little use elsewhere.
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
.Nm
generated each TypeScript declaration file without an error.
.It 1
No arguments were passed to
.Nm ,
or one of them references a non-regular file
.Pq directory, socket, FIFO, character device, etc .
.It 2
Required program
.Ql jsdoc
not found in
.Ev PATH .
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh EXAMPLES
Consider the following file that exports mathematical functions,
where the parameters of
.Fn angleTo
reference a JSDoc type defined solely via
.@ typedef :
.Bd -literal -offset 4n
/**
 * Measure the arctangent between two points.
 * @param {Point} a
 * @param {Point} b
 * @return {Number}
 */
export function angleTo(a, b){
	return radToDeg(Math.atan2(b[1] - a[1], a[0] - b[0]));
}
/**
 * Convert radians to degrees.
 * @param {Radians} value
 * @return {Degrees}
 */
export function radToDeg(value){
	return value * 180 / Math.PI;
}
/**
 * Pair of floats representing Cartesian coordinates.
 * @typedef  {Number[]} Point
 * @property {Number} x
 * @property {Number} y
 */
.Ed
.Pp
Running
.Bd -literal -compact -offset 4n
.Nm jg Cm typewrite \e
.Bd -unfilled -compact -offset 6n
.	Fl -header No \(dq// Generated file\(dq \e
.	Fl -declare Ar type Vt Radians number No \e
.	Fl -declare Ar type Vt Degrees number No \e
.	Ar angle-to.mjs
.Ed
.Ed
.Pp
will generate
.Pa angle-to.d.ts
with the following contents:
.Bd -literal -offset 4n
// Generated file
declare interface Point extends Array<number> {x: number; y: number}
export declare function angleTo(a: Point, b: Point): number;
export declare function radToDeg(value: Radians): Degrees;
export declare type Radians = number;
export declare type Degrees = number;
.Ed
.Pp
Check that generated declaration files are valid TypeScript syntax:
.Dl Cm tsc Fl -noEmit Ar angle-to.d.ts
.
